You're soon going to be picking up an Atari Lynx to play this game because if you don't want to play as the Valkyrie or the Wizard,

00:42:36.120 --> 00:42:40.320
too bad you can't play as the Warrior or the Elf anymore.

00:42:40.860 --> 00:42:43.060
Instead, you play as maybe a Samurai.

00:42:43.340 --> 00:42:48.900
Okay. What about a Punk Rocker or an Android or a Gunfighter or the Nerd?

00:42:49.440 --> 00:42:51.440
The Nerd. What's the Nerd do?

00:42:51.540 --> 00:42:53.600
I have no idea, but I've got to watch a video.

00:42:53.980 --> 00:42:57.380
Or the last choice and the one I would definitely pick, the Pirate.

00:42:57.720 --> 00:42:58.600
I do like that.

00:42:58.640 --> 00:43:02.060
I want that Pirate class, and I want to know what makes him different than the Nerd.

00:43:03.840 --> 00:43:05.480
Treasure probably makes him happy.

00:43:05.480 --> 00:43:08.660
I like that they're just doing – that's actually true.

00:43:08.800 --> 00:43:11.220
He gets more bonus experience from Treasure.

00:43:11.480 --> 00:43:16.360
I like that they're just doing different character classes to the same Gauntlet concept.

00:43:16.480 --> 00:43:22.300
They haven't rethought it and been like, no, it should have an overarching story and just be different.

00:43:23.100 --> 00:43:26.080
This is the water levels, and these are the jungle levels.

00:43:26.200 --> 00:43:27.840
They're just keeping it the same way.

00:43:28.040 --> 00:43:31.620
So after Gauntlet, the third encounter, how about Gauntlet 3?

00:43:32.740 --> 00:43:34.040
Okay. Yeah, that's true.

00:43:34.040 --> 00:43:37.640
Gauntlet 3, the final quest on home computers.

00:43:37.740 --> 00:43:39.360
That wasn't the last one, was it?

00:43:39.620 --> 00:43:40.580
It wasn't.

00:43:40.680 --> 00:43:44.740
Okay. It comes out in 1991, a year after Gauntlet the third.

00:43:46.400 --> 00:43:51.620
It's mostly the same, except for the new character classes are a rock man.

00:43:51.860 --> 00:43:54.500
Rock man. So not to be confused with a punk rocker.

00:43:54.840 --> 00:43:56.160
Is he a man made of rocks?

00:43:56.200 --> 00:43:57.480
He's a man made of rocks.

00:43:57.480 --> 00:44:00.140
Okay. As opposed to the punk rocker that was in the third encounter.

00:44:01.240 --> 00:44:07.360
Petrus. I don't know what Petrus is, but imagine that's some kind of fantasy species.

00:44:07.900 --> 00:44:09.620
Yeah. A dracolus.

00:44:10.640 --> 00:44:11.720
A lizard man.

00:44:13.140 --> 00:44:14.200
Oh, I see. Okay, okay.

00:44:14.320 --> 00:44:16.980
No, no. Petrus is the name of the rock man.

00:44:17.160 --> 00:44:17.980
Okay, I get it now.

00:44:18.820 --> 00:44:20.560
And dracolus is the lizard man.

00:44:20.980 --> 00:44:23.240
Then there's an ice man and a merman.

00:44:23.760 --> 00:44:24.800
Ooh. These are great classes.

00:44:24.800 --> 00:44:25.920
I would love to play as merman.

00:44:25.940 --> 00:44:28.640
When are we going to finally get- This is like Goonies 2.

00:44:28.880 --> 00:44:30.980
Yeah. Except for the mermaid.

00:44:31.260 --> 00:44:32.360
I might explain, though.

00:44:32.420 --> 00:44:33.380
Maybe they know each other.

00:44:33.480 --> 00:44:38.100
Yeah, that's true. And finally, it's like we're almost like, when is Gauntlet Ultimate going to happen?

00:44:38.120 --> 00:44:40.460
Where you get all the classes in the original Gauntlet.

00:44:40.600 --> 00:44:42.560
You know, like all these classes that were ever added.

00:44:42.700 --> 00:44:46.260
It's an idea. It's funny you asked that, because it's coming out next year.

00:44:46.440 --> 00:44:48.500
Great. Are you developing it?

00:44:48.560 --> 00:44:50.320
I am. Okay, fantastic.

00:44:50.580 --> 00:44:51.680
Go starting tonight.

00:44:51.780 --> 00:44:52.660
Fund my Kickstarter.

00:44:52.660 --> 00:44:55.380
I'm going to be a starter. Gauntlet 3, the final quest.

00:44:55.700 --> 00:44:59.740
It was an isometric perspective for the Gauntlet game.

00:45:00.020 --> 00:45:02.140
Two-player cooperative mode as well.

00:45:02.620 --> 00:45:06.220
Then on the PS2, this might be the version of the game Sean played.

00:45:06.400 --> 00:45:07.680
What was PS1? It was-

00:45:07.680 --> 00:45:08.840
But there is no PS1 game.

00:45:09.320 --> 00:45:10.360
Okay, it must have been PS2.

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:12.880
Gauntlet Seven Sorrows.

00:45:13.360 --> 00:45:17.680
And that's a follow-up to Gauntlet Legends and Gauntlet Dark Legacy on the arcade.

00:45:18.020 --> 00:45:20.340
And it finally adds online play.

00:45:21.020 --> 00:45:26.220
Yikes. So you can play Gauntlet online on the PS2 with a broadband connection.

00:45:27.300 --> 00:45:31.160
And the last one, Gauntlet Slayer Edition.

00:45:31.560 --> 00:45:34.720
This came out on PS4 in 2015.

00:45:34.940 --> 00:45:39.620
Oh, wow. And I just put my own note here, because I watch all the videos for these ones.

00:45:39.680 --> 00:45:42.160
I don't have Gauntlet Slayer Edition, so I just watched it.

00:45:42.400 --> 00:45:44.820
And I just wrote, it overstayed its welcome.

00:45:45.440 --> 00:45:47.980
Gauntlet Slayer Edition looks terrible.

00:45:48.820 --> 00:45:50.980
They didn't really update much.

00:45:51.140 --> 00:45:52.560
Does it have any microtransactions?

00:45:53.400 --> 00:45:56.280
You know, that might be what the Slayer thing is about.

00:45:56.520 --> 00:45:59.620
But no, it doesn't have microtransactions as far as I can tell.

00:45:59.780 --> 00:46:01.340
Probably it's online. Nice.

00:46:01.340 --> 00:46:08.480
But it doesn't look like they've thought about how they could change Gauntlet from 1985 to 2015.

00:46:08.940 --> 00:46:13.140
So what a sad 30th anniversary Gauntlet Slayer Edition was.

00:46:13.360 --> 00:46:23.720
Oh, well. Well, it's been more than 30 years now, but we're going to determine if Gauntlet on the NES is an essential game on our essential games list.

00:46:26.200 --> 00:46:35.180
Joe? I know there were some little flaws and it wasn't crazy at first about the time ticking down.

00:46:36.280 --> 00:46:38.700
But I think I want to throw this one an essential vote.

00:46:38.960 --> 00:46:43.540
I really like that it's bringing this co-op experience to the table that I didn't play.

00:46:44.500 --> 00:46:46.040
But I like it.

00:46:46.140 --> 00:46:48.300
I feel like I'm very interested in playing it.

00:46:48.440 --> 00:46:50.880
And playing it single player was pretty fun.

00:46:51.020 --> 00:47:00.460
And it brought like this Dungeon Crawler Explorer style is something new that I kind of want to go back and play it.

00:47:00.520 --> 00:47:02.940
I'm not sure I'll ever play through 100 levels of it.

00:47:03.040 --> 00:47:11.480
But with the password system, provided that the passwords all work, I don't mind kind of quote-unquote saving my progress and coming back and trying it again.

00:47:11.520 --> 00:47:13.260
So I'm going to give it an essential vote.

00:47:13.540 --> 00:47:14.880
All right. It's got one.

00:47:15.080 --> 00:47:16.800
It needs two.

00:47:17.100 --> 00:47:18.080
Two? Okay.

00:47:18.420 --> 00:47:20.020
I'm just making sure I have these rules right.

00:47:20.080 --> 00:47:22.360
I almost said three. Sean?

00:47:22.860 --> 00:47:33.820
So I'm sort of on the fence about this game because it definitely ticks all the boxes on how unique of an experience it is at this point in the NES's life cycle.

00:47:33.820 --> 00:47:43.480
But I think in order for me to put it on the essential games list, I personally have to enjoy playing it to some extent.

00:47:43.620 --> 00:47:51.320
And while I didn't hate it, and I have had some good things to say about it, it wasn't my favorite thing.

00:47:51.320 --> 00:47:56.640
So if this does become an essential game, I will not have my name attached to it.

00:47:57.400 --> 00:48:06.160
All right. And, you know, I think a lot of people are going to think that I'm going to vote not essential because I was pretty tough on the game.

00:48:06.320 --> 00:48:07.260
But I'm tough on every game.

00:48:07.380 --> 00:48:08.840
You never know where I'm going to go here.

00:48:08.840 --> 00:48:19.540
I will say one thing that I didn't touch upon because we just didn't get there is there's this diagonal shooting that is possible but is really finicky.

00:48:19.540 --> 00:48:27.940
And you have to, like, lock yourself into it in a way where it's not accurate but it's useful to be able to do diagonal shooting.

00:48:28.080 --> 00:48:29.280
And I hated that.

00:48:29.480 --> 00:48:32.860
That was, like, my least favorite thing was when I was in a position where I needed to do that.

00:48:32.960 --> 00:48:37.200
And the best practice was just to lock yourself in a corner of blocks.

00:48:37.320 --> 00:48:38.580
Yeah, you have to, like, walk into it.

00:48:38.960 --> 00:48:39.840
Didn't like that.

00:48:41.000 --> 00:48:44.300
So that has no sway in my essential game, but I just had to say that.

00:48:45.400 --> 00:48:47.000
Yeah, I mean, it's doing a lot of new things.

00:48:47.120 --> 00:48:50.480
And the cooperative mode was really cool to be playing two people at the same time.

00:48:51.740 --> 00:48:53.760
We did get to do that with Contra, though.

00:48:53.940 --> 00:48:56.460
And I know some people are like, oh, well, it wasn't that great in Contra.

00:48:56.520 --> 00:48:57.520
And I thought it was fantastic.

00:48:58.720 --> 00:49:00.360
So that isn't that new.

00:49:00.580 --> 00:49:04.780
The dungeon crawling thing was more satisfying for me when I was going through the dungeons in Legend of Zelda.

00:49:05.440 --> 00:49:08.220
And so for that case, I'm kind of removed from this one.

00:49:08.220 --> 00:49:10.080
So it's not going to get there for me.

00:49:10.300 --> 00:49:12.160
But, Joe, I respect you for putting it on the list.

00:49:12.300 --> 00:49:14.020
We'll make a note that you voted it essential.

00:49:14.380 --> 00:49:15.220
I respect you, too, Joe.

00:49:15.400 --> 00:49:16.480
I respect you.

00:49:16.700 --> 00:49:18.200
You guys are very agreeable.

00:49:19.220 --> 00:49:23.260
Even when we were disagreeing or when we agree, we speak like we disagree.

00:49:23.280 --> 00:49:24.480
You don't even know what it was about.

00:49:25.440 --> 00:49:26.920
I agree. Yeah.

00:49:26.920 --> 00:49:30.300
Cool. So do you agree that it won't be an essential game?

00:49:30.480 --> 00:49:31.360
I totally agree.

00:49:31.540 --> 00:49:34.320
I mean, I agree that it won't be, but I still wish it was.

00:49:34.540 --> 00:49:36.440
Got it. Okay. Maybe Gauntlet 2 will get there.

00:49:36.540 --> 00:49:38.900
Maybe. Yeah. If it improves.

00:49:39.500 --> 00:49:48.720
Why not? Yeah. I think for this game specifically, it seems like the arcade version would be awesome to

00:49:48.720 --> 00:49:49.900
one day get a hold of.

00:49:50.180 --> 00:49:55.220
And this NES one, the core gameplay loop didn't suck me in.

00:49:55.320 --> 00:49:59.880
And the actual combat wasn't satisfying.

00:50:00.200 --> 00:50:01.760
So that's why I took it off.

00:50:01.760 --> 00:50:05.380
I think it has a lot going for it that we haven't seen before, which is great.

00:50:05.760 --> 00:50:07.880
But maybe Gauntlet 2 will refine that.

00:50:08.180 --> 00:50:14.220
And if you know something about Gauntlet 2 listeners, why don't you write to us on the

00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:15.700
Twitter? Don't spoil it for us.

00:50:15.740 --> 00:50:18.500
At NostalgiaCast if you think that that one might make it essential.

00:50:18.760 --> 00:50:24.320
There was a time where we were talking about other games maybe becoming essential in their

00:50:24.320 --> 00:50:26.560
later iterations. And someone was like, no, don't waste your time.

00:50:26.700 --> 00:50:27.640
The next one's worse.

00:50:28.100 --> 00:50:29.200
I forgot which one that was.

00:50:29.200 --> 00:50:32.580
Maybe it was Akari Warriors, which definitely was true.

00:50:33.180 --> 00:50:37.040
Akari Warriors 2 was garbage and unfounded from the first one.

00:50:37.180 --> 00:50:40.860
Like it's really just like, I can't believe they're the same franchise.

00:50:41.180 --> 00:50:44.320
But we, Nostalgia, are a franchise.

00:50:44.360 --> 00:50:45.760
We do this every Friday.

00:50:45.760 --> 00:50:47.040
I hope you join us.

00:50:47.200 --> 00:50:50.000
I hope you write to us at NostalgiaCast on Twitter.

00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:52.640
Or you can write to me at Esposito Film on Twitter.

00:50:53.440 --> 00:50:57.740
Joe and Sean are always over my shoulder.

00:50:57.740 --> 00:50:59.040
Even right now.

00:50:59.040 --> 00:51:01.400
We record, we set up our mics over his shoulder.

00:51:01.420 --> 00:51:06.460
Don't be afraid that if you tweet at me or at NostalgiaCast that they won't see it.

00:51:06.600 --> 00:51:08.500
They see it. They're always looking.

00:51:09.040 --> 00:51:10.440
Yeah. Remember that time?

00:51:10.440 --> 00:51:11.540
I've seen your tax returns.

00:51:12.560 --> 00:51:13.680
Really? Yeah.

00:51:13.960 --> 00:51:19.780
Nice. Remember that time that we posted that Super Smash Brothers meme that had nothing to do

00:51:19.780 --> 00:51:21.580
with Nostalgia? That was Sean.

00:51:21.780 --> 00:51:24.360
Sean made that. So we are also memers.

00:51:24.780 --> 00:51:25.840
Sean's a professional memer.

00:51:25.840 --> 00:51:27.320
Sean does that for a living.

00:51:27.720 --> 00:51:32.280
You can contact me through Mike and I will make you a meme.

00:51:32.640 --> 00:51:37.000
I will make either, I'll make a meme for you or I'll make you into a meme.

00:51:37.120 --> 00:51:38.760
Yeah, there are really. For a nominal fee.

00:51:38.980 --> 00:51:40.520
There's not too many NES memes.

00:51:40.840 --> 00:51:41.860
It's true. Yeah.

00:51:42.540 --> 00:51:43.420
Why do you think that is?

00:51:43.920 --> 00:51:50.860
I think memes as we know them are a relatively new phenomenon and maybe not have existed so

00:51:50.860 --> 00:51:52.000
much in the NES days.

00:51:52.000 --> 00:51:53.660
But Nintendo is also very litigious.

00:51:54.040 --> 00:51:55.680
They see a meme, they go right after you.

